**Config file location (Windows):**
```
C:\Users\<USERNAME>\AppData\Roaming\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json
```

Open the file (create it if it doesn't exist) and add the server entry:

```json
{
 "mcpServers": {
 "uefi-<SUBJECT_SLUG>": {
 "command": "python",
 "args": ["-m", "src.server"],
 "cwd": "<UFABC_ROOT>\\uefi-<SUBJECT_SLUG>"
 }
 }
}
```

> **Important:** In Windows JSON paths, use double backslashes `\\` or forward slashes `/`.
> Example: `"E:\\Bibliotecas\\Documentos\\PROGRAMMING\\UEFIabc\\uefi-precalculus"`

Restart Claude Desktop after saving. The server name `uefi-<SUBJECT_SLUG>` will appear in Claude's tool list.

